# Copy to `.env.local` for local development.
#
# Three variables drive the BraDypUS v5 API client
# (src/components/Services/Database/Database.jsx):
#
#   REACT_APP_API_BASE  origin of the bdus instance, no trailing slash.
#                       Leave EMPTY to use the CRA dev proxy in package.json
#                       ("proxy": "http://localhost:8080") — this avoids CORS
#                       during `npm start`. Set a full URL only if you point at
#                       a remote instance (then that instance must allow CORS
#                       from http://localhost:3000 via BRADYPUS_CORS_ORIGIN).
#   REACT_APP_API_KEY   a read-privilege API key issued by that instance
#                       (bdus: Config → API keys). Required — every endpoint
#                       the atlas uses needs it.
#   REACT_APP_APP       bdus application id. Always `paths`.
#
# Production values live in the committed .env.production; the prod key is a
# GitHub Actions secret (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml).

REACT_APP_API_BASE=
REACT_APP_API_KEY=
REACT_APP_APP=paths
